WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.770
Well, there's a ship with some character to it.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.170
We're sailing on this junk?!
It'll sink before we step foot on it!

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:19.050
Sorry. It had to be an abandoned ship or the city officials would take notice.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:25.020
You made the right choice. It's enough that you were able to get us a ship.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.690
I'm glad to hear that.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.930
It should get you where you need to go.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.730
This is the least I could do to support the Ignauts.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.220
Thank you.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.960
All right! Let's climb aboard!

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.270
Quit sulking! Come on, let's go!

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.610
All right already!

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.710
Hurry it up, slow poke!

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.110
Quit shoving me!

00:00:50.980 --> 00:01:00.980
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:11.060
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:21.440
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:31.440
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:41.620
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.140
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:52.140 --> 00:02:02.140
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.820
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.210
Got him!

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.660
Enough!

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:53.340
Felix! This isn't a real fight!
Didn't I tell you not to use Warp Relics?

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.600
It could have been dangerous if I hadn't.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.850
It's pretty amazing that such a little kid can keep up with Felix.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.780
But I'm better than him...

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.740
Those guys are way too active for being on a ship...

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.050
Seasick? You're pathetic...

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.260
Gimme a break. This is my first time on a ship, all right?

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.900
If it wasn't so rickety maybe it wouldn't rock so much...

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.970
Are you okay?

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.800
If you're seasick, you should try some of these...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.580
Too spicy!

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.920
They're chili peppers.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.820
They can help treat nausea.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.290
I thought I was gonna die...

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.090
But I don't feel that sick anymore!

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.490
That's good to hear.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.090
Anyhow, where's Emilio at?

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.500
Hmm. I haven't seen him for a while now...

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:59.500
"8: Lone Isle"

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.350
What's with that face? You look awful.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.850
What face?

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.340
I'm perfectly fine.
Don't clump me together with Shun.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:23.090
You really think you can tame the Zoozians?

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:27.090
We're not trying to tame them.
We're getting their help.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.800
You don't seem pleased.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.360
Of course not. Did you forget all the allies of ours they hurt?

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.710
Not all Zoozians are like those guys.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:43.010
In fact, most of them are similar to us.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.780
There's nothing but rough waters ahead.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:53.060
The Zoozians were chased to that island specifically so they couldn't escape.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.960
It's like a naturally occurring prison.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.460
Can this old ship even make it there?

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.330
It'll be a rough ride for a spoiled prince like you.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:03.320
Don't call me that!

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.380
You're lucky I'm always around to save your ass.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.910
Shut up! I didn't ask for your help!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.190
I-I take it back!

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:29.560
Don't let go! Don't let me go, Prince Emilio!

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.660
Quit fighting and help each other.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.050
It's a bit rough out here...

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.890
It certainly is.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.090
The storm broke one of the boards on the hull.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.620
We'll sink if we don't fix it.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:04.790
Maybe my Warp Relic can hold her together.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.590
Is it going to be worth all this trouble?

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.150
We somehow... made it... alive.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.490
You're acting like a baby.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:37.930
Your face... is paler... than mine.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.420
Shut up. My head throbs when you talk.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.740
We're safe now, Falarion.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.970
The ship's in no shape to sail now...

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.010
If we can't get the help of the Zoozians...

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.580
...without a ship, our journey pretty much ends here.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.950
Sad but true.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:01.120
We're always walking a tightrope, aren't we?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.750
You've got that right.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.950
But that's fine with me, as long as we're making progress.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.920
Nothing ever gets these guys down...

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.960
Who was that?!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.770
Zoozians!

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.510
What a warm welcome.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.510
Why the hell did you come here?

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:32.850
They're enemies!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.340
Quit it, Mischa.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.340
Stay calm. We didn't come here to fight.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.630
Are you the chief of the Zoozians here?

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.300
We need to talk...

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:08.380
Wh-What the hell is gonna happen to us?!

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.490
Not very kind to your guests?

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:17.330
Isn't this a bit too much?
We only came here to--

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.890
Silence.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:23.430
The only reason we didn't bind you is because you're part Zoozian.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:26.400
But here, we do things our own way.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.100
You have no say here.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:33.340
Hey! What gives?
Aren't we kinda screwed here?!

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:35.680
Isn't it obvious?

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.510
Seeing all that's happened between Endras and Zoozians,

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:41.450
anyone could have guessed it would end up like this.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.290
What could Demetrio possibly be thinking?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.620
You're not even slightly afraid in a situation like this?

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:52.930
That's different than all the others that cower at our sight.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.770
We've heard rumors, even as far as here.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.970
You must be the Ignauts.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.370
A band of revolutionaries led by a man named Demetrio.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:07.210
I'm honored that you remembered my name.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:11.410
What do you Ignauts want with us?

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.610
We need you Zoozians... to lend us your strength.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:20.720
We can't hope to compete with the king's might without you.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.560
Those Endras want us to help?

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:26.960
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:35.800
Supposing we help you, what do we have to gain?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.100
Freedom and your dignity.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:46.350
If Delzaine falls, I promise you a world where Zoozians are no longer oppressed.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.280
You promise?

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:52.960
Since when have you Endras ever upheld a promise you've made to us?

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:57.690
You just plan to use us so you can become king yourself.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:00.860
I have no intentions of becoming king.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:02.660
I can't trust your word.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:11.940
What did the Endras do to make the Zoozians so mad at them?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:17.510
The Zoozians... are physically superior to the Endras.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:23.720
For many years they were forced into the most dangerous and demanding work.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.660
They were used and tossed aside like mere tools.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:32.230
The ones who resisted or became ill or injured and unable to work...

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.720
...were sent away to this island.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.000
That's awful...

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.960
Their mistrust and disdain for people is well deserved.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:47.640
I know...

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:52.080
If you want our help,
I have one condition for you...

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.220
Condition?

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:56.150
Give up your life.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.100
His life?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.870
What do you mean?

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:18.330
If you give up your life, we'll listen to your request.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.550
Y-You can't--

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:27.040
I'm only talking to him.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:34.420
If you refuse, then we won't help.
Furthermore, we'll kill all your friends...

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.690
...and let only you live.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:46.370
If you believe in a cause, your life is a small price to pay to achieve it.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.240
This is bullshit!

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:52.540
If you touch Demetrio, you're dead.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:57.250
Felix, Mischa! Don't be so reckless.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:01.550
There's no point! Demetrio is the one reason we're all here!

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:03.920
Demetrio, you mustn't agree.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:10.890
Demetrio, don't do something stupid!
Without you, nothing will ever happen!

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.500
No. That's where you're wrong.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.500
Huh?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:20.000
The seeds of revolt to bring down the king are already growing.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.470
It will happen eventually, even without me.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.980
With the support of the Zoozians, there will be no stopping it.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.410
You can't...

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.910
Demetrio...

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.150
Go ahead and kill me.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:36.990
But promise me this...

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:43.190
In exchange for my head, you support the rebellion and harm none of my friends.

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:45.320
If you can't guarantee me that...

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.460
You have my word.

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:13.950
You guys...

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.890
What are you doing?

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:20.000
You're a Zoozian, aren't you?

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.830
I won't allow you to kill this man.

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:26.570
Kill me in his place.
Let him go and kill me instead.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.970
If that's not enough, take my life as well...

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:31.140
Let's execute both of them!

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:32.800
Yeah! Kill them all!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.220
I'm the one in charge here.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.020
Do you have a death wish?

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:57.430
I respect your choice. Let us talk alone.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.540
We're saved...

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.540
I thought we were goners for sure back there!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:13.780
They've untied us, so at least we've gained a little of their trust.

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:19.960
But we're not allowed to leave either, so they must be keeping an eye on us.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.720
Will Demetrio be okay?

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:28.430
If something happens to him, they'll pay for it...

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:32.270
He'll be fine, I'm sure. He always is...

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:40.940
What? Kids?

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.380
H-Hey!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.620
What's going on?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.120
They're afraid of us?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:15:01.400
But why? Zoozians are violent and tougher than us...

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:04.490
And that's exactly why they're persecuted.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:10.510
Even if they're stronger, there aren't nearly as many of them.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:14.110
They're no match for all the Endras and their weapons.

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:18.310
So they're oppressed and treated like slaves.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.840
The Zoozians here know what it means to suffer.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:34.590
Saké is precious on this island. It's served to guests as the highest form of respect.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.000
It's really good.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:46.370
That's the second time you've risked your life.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.050
There could have been poison in that drink.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:56.180
But without accepting my token of friendship, you cannot hope to negotiate.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:59.150
So you drank it knowing it might be fatal.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:03.560
It shows that your ideals are more important than your life.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.130
I never worried about it being poisoned.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:11.830
You said we were going to talk. You're not the kind of man to go back on his word.

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:18.140
I haven't introduced myself yet.
The name's Gradido.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.200
I'm the chief of the Zoozians on this island.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:25.250
You came here to get the help of us Zoozians...

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.540
...and I approve.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:28.980
Thank you!

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:33.190
However, I want to ask more about your intentions.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:36.020
Sure, what is it?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:40.660
You say you want our support, but for what purpose?

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.260
To fight against the king's army?

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:47.240
No. I don't plan on having you fight.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:50.940
I want the revolution to succeed without spilling anyone's blood.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.580
You're naïve... but in a good way.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:17:01.050
What we need is a display of our strength and number of supporters.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:05.190
They won't negotiate unless you're their equals...

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:09.560
So that's why you need us to be on your side.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:11.030
Right.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.360
One more question...

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:17.870
When you say you don't intend to be king, what do you mean?

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.240
Exactly how it sounds.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.570
Society will collapse without someone to rule.

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.270
Do you plan to bring down society itself?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.810
No.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.750
Someone other than me will be king.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.650
Other than you?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.580
Even if I were to become king...

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:41.060
...people will believe I revolted to obtain power, no matter what I say.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.830
A country can't be built on such doubts.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:49.430
Instead, I'll pick a suitable king who treats everyone the same,

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:53.270
regardless of wealth, race, or standing.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.900
Do you have someone in mind?

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.430
Not yet...

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:09.320
Hey! There you are...

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.750
Shun?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:15.760
The Zoozians are going to lend us a hand after all.

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:18.630
I guess Demetrio was able to talk them into it.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:21.460
What's wrong?

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:25.800
You should be happy. We're one step closer to bringing down Delzaine.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.670
So why do you look so confused?

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:29.940
Shun...

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.170
I never really left the castle before all this happened.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.170
Yeah, you sure lived in a cave.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:37.810
I did.

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:40.010
I'm completely ignorant of this world.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:46.350
The kids in the port city...
The Zoozians on this island...

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:52.790
Before, Demetrio asked me what
I would do after I killed the king.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:56.530
Yeah. That was back when we first met him.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:19:03.370
I thought nothing else mattered as long as I could avenge my father.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.310
But that's not really the end...

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:14.720
If Delzaine dies, the country will continue.
Its people still have to live on...

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:19.720
Shun... You lived in a completely different place than Endora, right?

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.820
Yeah. Pretty much.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:24.690
What was it like where you lived?

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.600
What was it like for everybody?

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.730
This is like the first time you've ever asked about my world.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.400
It really is...

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.100
Can you tell me?

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:36.940
Well...

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:41.710
Compared to here, it's a lot more convenient and easier to live.

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:44.250
The technology there is way more advanced.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:45.050
It is?

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:49.350
Yeah. You know all those weird gadgets Pascal always makes?

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:52.850
Everyone has stuff like that they use every day.

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:56.460
Everyone has inventions just like Pascal's?

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:58.960
That sounds like a disaster...

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:02.060
We all get used to new technology pretty quickly.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:04.270
I can't even imagine...

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:09.570
It's peaceful; there's, like, no discrimination, and there's food enough for everyone.

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.910
It sounds like an ideal world.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.770
Yeah. I guess it does...

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.110
What's wrong?

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.050
Nothing. Don't worry about it.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:33.290
Gradido is joining up with them, it seems.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:35.760
Annoying...

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.330
Really? That human hater?

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:41.940
That'll be a powerful ally for 'em.

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.270
There's something else... An interesting find.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.940
What is it?

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:52.110
The boy who gave you that scar...
He's from the surface.

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:53.600
That brat?!

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:58.190
What now? We gonna report back to Delzaine?

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.320
No... There's no need for that.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.930
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:09.700
<i>Took a long way to get here</i>

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.670
<i>Had to go around and around</i>

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:17.810
<i>But every single road I've taken</i>

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:21.680
<i>Made me who I am today</i>

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:28.640
<i>go my way go my way</i>

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:40.130
<i>The world will show you there's tomorrow</i>

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:48.660
<i>Look up to the blue sky and you will see</i>

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:57.550
<i>I try to be better than who I was yesterday</i>

00:21:57.550 --> 00:22:04.720
<i>So I can see you with a smile on my face today</i>

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:09.990
<i>Now what should we get into today?</i>

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:18.600
<i>The scent of summer arouses my heart</i>

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.740
<i>And I can't seem to find the right words to tell you</i>

00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:28.200
<i>That I love you just the way you are</i>

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:39.950
"Episode 9: Father and Child"

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:39.950
Next episode, "Father and Child."
